acceptance_criteria:
- Terraform module (registry-style) that can be used in private VPC stacks to: configure KMS/HSM endpoint, TLS/mTLS certs, metrics exporter, and a configurable healthcheck resource;
- Module exposes variables for failover KMS (cloud fallback), rotation windows, and canary metrics labels;
- Module emits Prometheus metrics/OTLP config that the Console can scrape or ingest (docs + example);
- Healthcheck supports liveness/readiness semantics (fast failover threshold + configurable retries);
- Includes an "upgrade_mode" variable enabling dual-write or read-only read-after-write strategies for migrations;
- Unit tests for TF module (terratest or kitchen-terraform) and a smoke deployment runbook;
- Security review checklist completed and PR merged into infra repo.

test_plan:
- Unit tests: terratest suite that validates module outputs and conditional logic;
- Integration: deploy to staging VPC with a software HSM emulator + cloud-kms fallback, run healthcheck probe, assert metrics appear in OTLP exporter;
- Chaos test: simulate HSM latency and transient failures to validate failover thresholds and circuit breaker behaviour;
- Upgrade dry-run: enable dual-write, exercise canary traffic, assert no data loss and Console shows key parity metrics;
- Security: run static scanning on TF, verify IAM roles adhere to least privilege.
